1
00:00:00,083 --> 00:00:01,707
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,708 --> 00:00:03,041
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,125 --> 00:00:05,291
(Episode 76)

4
00:00:06,208 --> 00:00:08,416
- Mom!
- What's gotten into you?

5
00:00:08,916 --> 00:00:11,875
Why are you treating me
with such disrespect?

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,500
I'm not disrespecting you.

7
00:00:13,541 --> 00:00:15,666
Then what would you call it? Respect?

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,750
I asked you for some time.

9
00:00:17,833 --> 00:00:20,333
Time before I can face Ji Ni again.

10
00:00:20,375 --> 00:00:21,916
- Is that too much to ask?
- I know.

11
00:00:22,041 --> 00:00:24,125
- But I had no choice...
- What?

12
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:26,125
Are you two expecting a child?

13
00:00:26,583 --> 00:00:29,416
If that's the case,
let's hurry things along. But if not,

14
00:00:30,041 --> 00:00:32,333
it hasn't even been a month
since I asked for some time,

15
00:00:32,416 --> 00:00:34,291
and now you're telling me you proposed?

16
00:00:34,666 --> 00:00:36,958
Is this how a son treats his mom?

17
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:41,791
I know I'm not the perfect mom, but still.
How could you?

18
00:00:43,791 --> 00:00:45,000
I'm sorry.

19
00:00:45,166 --> 00:00:47,666
Don't apologize if you don't mean it.

20
00:00:48,916 --> 00:00:50,750
Tell me. What's the reason?

21
00:00:50,916 --> 00:00:51,958
I'm anxious.

22
00:00:52,125 --> 00:00:54,791
- Afraid Ji Ni might change her mind?
- Yes.

23
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,290
The one who loves more
is always the one who holds on tighter.

24
00:00:57,291 --> 00:01:00,040
So you're afraid
she might change her mind?

25
00:01:00,041 --> 00:01:02,500
I told you I needed some time!

26
00:01:03,083 --> 00:01:05,958
I asked for time to get ready,
and you spring this on me?

27
00:01:06,208 --> 00:01:08,500
Well, your mom's right about that.

28
00:01:08,833 --> 00:01:11,000
Ji Hu, don't rush into this...

29
00:01:11,125 --> 00:01:13,041
You're lying when you say you need time.

30
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:15,666
You're just using that time
to find a way to reject her.

31
00:01:16,083 --> 00:01:17,250
Am I wrong?

32
00:01:18,083 --> 00:01:19,125
Am I?

33
00:01:19,291 --> 00:01:21,375
Well, that's...

34
00:01:21,791 --> 00:01:24,583
Mom, Do Hee's leaving tomorrow.

35
00:01:24,916 --> 00:01:27,458
I want to put everything back
where it belongs.

36
00:01:27,958 --> 00:01:29,416
Please help me.

37
00:01:37,041 --> 00:01:39,458
- Honey.
- Why aren't you saying anything?

38
00:01:39,875 --> 00:01:43,083
You used to command an entire army.
Why can't you control your own son?

39
00:01:43,666 --> 00:01:46,040
Am I really going to have to sit
across from that mistress...

40
00:01:46,041 --> 00:01:49,000
and call her my in-law?

41
00:01:50,416 --> 00:01:54,875
I'm the one being humiliated here.
Why aren't you saying anything?

42
00:02:14,333 --> 00:02:15,666
I'll take care of it.

43
00:02:24,208 --> 00:02:26,833
- Where's Ji Hu?
- I think he's gone upstairs to his room.

44
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:34,375
- Have a drink too.
- Thank you.

45
00:02:37,958 --> 00:02:41,416
Is this because of Ji Hu's marriage?

46
00:02:43,291 --> 00:02:45,625
Your wife seems to be having a hard time.

47
00:02:49,791 --> 00:02:52,833
Have you made up your mind
about Ji Ni, General?

48
00:02:57,041 --> 00:02:58,916
Ji Hu knows he was adopted.

49
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:04,790
How?

50
00:03:04,791 --> 00:03:07,416
I guess that woman went to see Ji Hu too.

51
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:12,375
How did I not consider that might happen?

52
00:03:13,875 --> 00:03:16,208
We were all so shocked at the time.

53
00:03:16,791 --> 00:03:18,190
How could something like this happen...

54
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:23,500
- What about your wife?
- She can't find out. It'll be a disaster.

55
00:03:23,791 --> 00:03:25,520
So that's why you've been
acting this way...

56
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:30,500
- I'm sorry.
- What do you have to be sorry for?

57
00:03:31,791 --> 00:03:36,000
I should've killed Na Se Ri
along with Cha Min Ki back then.

58
00:03:36,791 --> 00:03:39,583
Then Ji Ni would never have ended up here.

59
00:03:39,916 --> 00:03:41,708
There's no point dwelling on that.

60
00:03:44,594 --> 00:03:47,844
If I only look at Ji Ni,
she seems better than Do Hee.

61
00:03:48,458 --> 00:03:51,416
No, she's just like her mom.

62
00:03:52,708 --> 00:03:54,458
Ji Hu deserves better.

63
00:04:03,333 --> 00:04:07,083
- Did you tell her?
- Yes. She's thrilled.

64
00:04:07,666 --> 00:04:10,291
But she keeps insisting
we move in together.

65
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:12,510
I wouldn't mind living together.

66
00:04:12,763 --> 00:04:14,000
Why are you so against it, Ji Ni?

67
00:04:14,052 --> 00:04:16,223
After everything you've been through,
how can you say that?

68
00:04:18,708 --> 00:04:21,000
What do your parents think?

69
00:04:21,166 --> 00:04:23,375
They're shocked, of course.

70
00:04:23,666 --> 00:04:25,583
They said we should take things slowly.

71
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:28,039
Then let's do that.

72
00:04:28,041 --> 00:04:29,958
Don't make things uncomfortable
for your parents.

73
00:04:30,041 --> 00:04:31,958
- I'm fine with it...
- Like I said earlier,

74
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,666
I want you to feel at ease
as soon as possible, Ji Ni.

75
00:04:35,083 --> 00:04:37,958
So don't let your doubts get to you.
Just stick by my side.

76
00:04:38,125 --> 00:04:40,875
I'll clear every obstacle
in our way. Okay?

77
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:43,750
Why are you so quiet?

78
00:04:44,750 --> 00:04:45,916
Okay.

79
00:04:46,958 --> 00:04:48,458
Get some sleep. See you tomorrow.

80
00:04:49,214 --> 00:04:50,214
I love you.

81
00:05:00,791 --> 00:05:01,791
Yes?

82
00:05:03,791 --> 00:05:06,291
Ji Hu, I heard you went to Seo Chon today.

83
00:05:06,458 --> 00:05:08,416
I just went to pick up Ji Ni.

84
00:05:08,791 --> 00:05:10,625
Did you happen to see Seung Woo?

85
00:05:10,833 --> 00:05:12,166
He isn't answering my calls.

86
00:05:12,625 --> 00:05:15,291
He was at the cafe
with Do Hee again today.

87
00:05:15,375 --> 00:05:17,000
I just don't understand him.

88
00:05:17,208 --> 00:05:19,875
Don't worry.
She'll be going to England soon.

89
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:22,915
Ji Ni said she'd forgive Do Hee
on one condition,

90
00:05:22,916 --> 00:05:24,875
that she stop contacting Seung Woo.

91
00:05:25,791 --> 00:05:27,625
If she agrees, Ji Ni won't press charges
and will let her leave.

92
00:05:27,666 --> 00:05:28,666
Ji Ni said that?

93
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,750
That alone would be such a relief.

94
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:36,833
Uncle knows, but he isn't saying anything?

95
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:40,083
He's acting strange.

96
00:05:40,416 --> 00:05:42,750
He gets angry, saying I only care
about Seo Chon.

97
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:47,458
I married him because I thought
he was understanding and kindhearted,

98
00:05:48,250 --> 00:05:51,416
- but I guess that was all an act.
- I'm sure that's not true.

99
00:05:51,625 --> 00:05:53,583
I'm telling you, it is.

100
00:05:53,708 --> 00:05:56,958
Even this morning, he was talking
about grounds for divorce or something.

101
00:05:57,208 --> 00:05:59,166
Can you believe that?

102
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:01,625
You have a lot on your mind,

103
00:06:01,666 --> 00:06:04,541
so maybe he's trying to distract you
and take your mind off things.

104
00:06:05,125 --> 00:06:08,041
No one understands how anxious I feel.

105
00:06:08,958 --> 00:06:10,708
Only Ji Ni understands me.

106
00:06:11,833 --> 00:06:15,333
I proposed thanks to you, Aunt.

107
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:19,208
Really? Good for you!

108
00:06:19,875 --> 00:06:21,500
I'm so grateful to you.

109
00:06:21,625 --> 00:06:24,250
Of course, I still have a long way to go.

110
00:06:25,208 --> 00:06:27,390
- Your mom?
- Yes.

111
00:06:27,708 --> 00:06:30,957
She's getting a daughter-in-law
like Ji Ni,

112
00:06:30,958 --> 00:06:32,590
so what does she have to complain about?

113
00:06:33,875 --> 00:06:35,416
I'm the one who's worried.

114
00:06:35,541 --> 00:06:38,541
Who knows when the daughter-in-law
who left home will come back?

115
00:06:39,083 --> 00:06:41,832
And my younger son seems completely blind
to what's going on.

116
00:06:41,833 --> 00:06:44,458
Why does he feel so sorry
for Do Hee, anyway?

117
00:06:45,375 --> 00:06:47,625
Get some rest.

118
00:06:49,666 --> 00:06:50,875
- Get some rest too.
- Okay.

119
00:07:01,083 --> 00:07:05,375
I didn't tell Aunt what happened
in Seo Chon earlier.

120
00:07:05,750 --> 00:07:07,832
She's already so worried about Seung Woo.

121
00:07:07,833 --> 00:07:08,833
(Ji Ni)

122
00:07:14,083 --> 00:07:17,083
Okay, I understand. I'll tell her later.

123
00:07:27,791 --> 00:07:30,500
Why are you so late? You didn't even call.

124
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,708
I was sorting the herbs.

125
00:07:33,791 --> 00:07:35,541
Am I the only one who ever calls?

126
00:07:35,625 --> 00:07:36,875
What's wrong with you calling me?

127
00:07:37,041 --> 00:07:39,375
You were probably worrying
about Seung Woo again.

128
00:07:40,415 --> 00:07:42,783
No. I was waiting for you.

129
00:07:44,291 --> 00:07:45,333
What about dinner?

130
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:48,958
I'll just go to bed.

131
00:07:49,541 --> 00:07:50,978
Are you still upset?

132
00:07:51,083 --> 00:07:54,625
No. When have I ever been upset?

133
00:07:55,125 --> 00:07:56,416
I'm sorry.

134
00:07:56,458 --> 00:07:58,666
I know what you're trying to say, Sa Bin.

135
00:07:59,125 --> 00:08:02,125
- You really do?
- Of course I do.

136
00:08:03,166 --> 00:08:05,250
How about kimchi fried rice?

137
00:08:06,166 --> 00:08:07,958
Sure.

138
00:08:10,250 --> 00:08:12,333
Go wash up. I'll call you.

139
00:08:40,958 --> 00:08:43,833
Are you drinking? Without any snacks?

140
00:08:44,625 --> 00:08:47,208
Lieutenant No went to get something.

141
00:08:48,708 --> 00:08:52,228
Sa Bin's dinner is running late,
so I'm making kimchi fried rice.

142
00:08:52,416 --> 00:08:54,041
Would you like me to make some soup too?

143
00:08:54,333 --> 00:08:55,916
I'd appreciate that.

144
00:09:01,208 --> 00:09:02,208
Yeong Ju.

145
00:09:03,541 --> 00:09:06,458
You know Ji Hu proposed to Ji Ni, right?

146
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,941
Yes. I just heard.

147
00:09:12,232 --> 00:09:14,805
You and Ji Ni haven't exactly had
the best relationship.

148
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:17,583
So how can you look after her
like she's your own niece?

149
00:09:18,208 --> 00:09:20,708
Of course, I've heard
about what happened before.

150
00:09:21,208 --> 00:09:25,743
But I imagine those things
aren't easy to forgive.

151
00:09:32,058 --> 00:09:34,839
Ji Ni hasn't done anything wrong.

152
00:09:35,166 --> 00:09:37,499
What's there to forgive?

153
00:09:38,666 --> 00:09:41,333
At first, I said a lot
of hurtful things too.

154
00:09:41,541 --> 00:09:43,041
That's why I'm scared.

155
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:46,791
It'd be frightening if things turned out
the way I said they would.

156
00:09:47,583 --> 00:09:49,416
You're a truly good person, Yeong Ju.

157
00:09:51,875 --> 00:09:52,875
Joong Bin.

158
00:09:53,791 --> 00:09:56,416
I know Sun Kyung is against this,

159
00:09:56,500 --> 00:10:01,375
so I'm hesitant to say this.
I don't want to overstep.

160
00:10:02,858 --> 00:10:04,632
Please just see Ji Ni for who she is.

161
00:10:05,375 --> 00:10:09,375
Maybe because she's been through so much,
she's more careful and thoughtful...

162
00:10:09,875 --> 00:10:14,083
than any other girl her age.
You know that.

163
00:10:16,458 --> 00:10:20,208
Kids these days expect their parents
to give them a privileged life.

164
00:10:20,541 --> 00:10:23,916
And many parents hope their children
will become their jackpot...

165
00:10:24,166 --> 00:10:26,666
whether they pursue sports or the arts.

166
00:10:27,708 --> 00:10:30,958
Ji Hu and Ji Ni seem
genuinely sincere about each other.

167
00:10:31,333 --> 00:10:32,916
That's what makes them so lovely.

168
00:10:34,474 --> 00:10:35,474
Joong Bin.

169
00:10:36,541 --> 00:10:41,916
Please put aside your prejudices
about Ji Ni and support them.

170
00:10:43,625 --> 00:10:46,375
Would you like a drink, Yeong Ju?

171
00:10:47,833 --> 00:10:49,833
Yes, please.

172
00:11:01,541 --> 00:11:02,666
Cheers.

173
00:11:58,166 --> 00:11:59,541
(Ji Hu)

174
00:12:05,782 --> 00:12:06,979
Did you sleep well?

175
00:12:08,099 --> 00:12:09,099
Ji Ni.

176
00:12:10,191 --> 00:12:12,066
What's wrong? Did something happen?

177
00:12:12,750 --> 00:12:14,000
Well...

178
00:12:14,583 --> 00:12:16,125
My mom left home.

179
00:12:17,083 --> 00:12:18,166
What?

180
00:12:20,125 --> 00:12:23,583
Since the day I met you,
I may have fallen short as a mom,

181
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,250
but I did the best I could.

182
00:12:26,791 --> 00:12:30,791
I'm deeply hurt and feel like
my life has been a failure.

183
00:12:32,208 --> 00:12:34,583
I won't oppose your marriage anymore.

184
00:12:35,083 --> 00:12:36,958
Work things out with your dad.

185
00:12:37,291 --> 00:12:39,625
Let's meet again
after some time has passed.

186
00:12:40,708 --> 00:12:42,708
She's gone this far because of me.

187
00:12:43,291 --> 00:12:44,791
This isn't your fault.

188
00:12:45,166 --> 00:12:47,041
I deliberately said things
to hurt her feelings.

189
00:12:47,541 --> 00:12:48,958
I wanted her to give up.

190
00:12:50,666 --> 00:12:53,708
I told her I wouldn't give up,
so she should be the one to give up.

191
00:12:54,916 --> 00:12:57,708
- It's my fault.
- What do we do now?

192
00:13:04,708 --> 00:13:06,958
Don't be afraid. I'll handle it.

193
00:13:07,875 --> 00:13:11,000
Let's set a date for our families to meet
and call my mom.

194
00:13:11,666 --> 00:13:14,083
Otherwise, we'll miss our chance again
and end up going in circles.

195
00:13:14,465 --> 00:13:15,715
No.

196
00:13:15,916 --> 00:13:18,958
Tell me where your mom might go.
I'll look for her.

197
00:13:19,041 --> 00:13:20,583
You don't know my mom.

198
00:13:21,458 --> 00:13:23,155
There's a side of her
that's like a little child.

199
00:13:27,257 --> 00:13:28,382
Ji Ni.

200
00:13:29,958 --> 00:13:34,416
The guilt of believing that
my birth broke up a family...

201
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,291
It's been a heavy burden
to carry all my life.

202
00:13:39,333 --> 00:13:42,499
I don't want to add the burden
of causing your mom such despair...

203
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:44,208
to everything I'm already carrying.

204
00:13:45,291 --> 00:13:47,333
Let's do everything we can.

205
00:14:03,041 --> 00:14:05,333
Think of him as your own child
and raise him.

206
00:14:05,625 --> 00:14:08,457
- Never let Joong Bin find out.
- I don't want to.

207
00:14:08,458 --> 00:14:10,583
How can I adopt a child?

208
00:14:10,666 --> 00:14:13,333
What? I told you not to call it adoption.

209
00:14:13,416 --> 00:14:15,041
Don't you dare make a mistake.

210
00:14:15,166 --> 00:14:17,250
He's your child. You gave birth to him.

211
00:14:17,458 --> 00:14:20,333
There's still time before Joong Bin's
ship comes back.

212
00:14:20,583 --> 00:14:23,166
In the meantime, say you gave birth
and have been raising the baby.

213
00:14:24,166 --> 00:14:25,625
Enough. I can't do this.

214
00:14:25,875 --> 00:14:28,000
I'll tell him everything
and get a divorce.

215
00:14:28,041 --> 00:14:29,208
I'll live on my own.

216
00:14:29,666 --> 00:14:31,583
As if you could live on your own.

217
00:14:31,708 --> 00:14:33,708
What can you even do?
And you think you can get divorced?

218
00:14:33,958 --> 00:14:37,125
All you know how to do is spend money
and take care of your looks.

219
00:14:37,166 --> 00:14:38,166
Mom!

220
00:14:39,416 --> 00:14:40,541
You were wrong, Mom.

221
00:14:41,250 --> 00:14:42,541
He's someone else's child after all.

222
00:14:42,583 --> 00:14:44,276
And look how he's turned on me.

223
00:14:46,208 --> 00:14:47,291
This is all your fault, Mom!

224
00:15:22,833 --> 00:15:23,833
Are you leaving now?

225
00:15:26,083 --> 00:15:27,750
Forget the door code.

226
00:15:28,291 --> 00:15:31,166
But why did you come?
We already said our goodbyes.

227
00:15:31,541 --> 00:15:34,458
Are you really going to wait
until I get married to come back?

228
00:15:34,791 --> 00:15:37,666
Who knows? Ask Ji Ni.

229
00:15:39,708 --> 00:15:41,208
You're sad to see me go, aren't you?

230
00:15:43,291 --> 00:15:47,333
Thank you for putting up with
all my whining and tears.

231
00:15:48,791 --> 00:15:52,541
You made me feel like I mattered.
It meant a lot to me.

232
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,083
Now go live like you matter.

233
00:15:55,583 --> 00:15:57,791
I took your side,

234
00:15:58,333 --> 00:16:00,625
and my family just misunderstood me.

235
00:16:03,208 --> 00:16:04,750
I want to leave too.

236
00:16:06,625 --> 00:16:08,833
Actually, when I quit
the broadcasting station,

237
00:16:09,250 --> 00:16:12,500
I thought about studying
documentary filmmaking abroad.

238
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,333
But O Reum got sick,
so I couldn't bring it up. And here I am.

239
00:16:16,833 --> 00:16:17,833
Really?

240
00:16:18,958 --> 00:16:20,833
I don't care where you go.

241
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,458
Just don't come to England.

242
00:16:23,125 --> 00:16:25,500
You used to cling to me,
but now you're keeping your distance.

243
00:16:26,208 --> 00:16:28,291
So I'm no use to you anymore?

244
00:16:28,333 --> 00:16:30,750
As Na Ji Ni's brother,
you're only useful to me here.

245
00:16:30,958 --> 00:16:32,750
What would I do with you in England?

246
00:16:32,958 --> 00:16:34,541
I'd just get an earful from Dad.

247
00:16:35,541 --> 00:16:37,249
If you leave, go somewhere else.

248
00:16:37,250 --> 00:16:39,125
You used me
because I was Na Ji Ni's brother,

249
00:16:39,375 --> 00:16:41,093
and now you're getting rid of me
because I'm Ji Ni's brother?

250
00:16:43,666 --> 00:16:45,541
Stop reading so much into everything.

251
00:16:46,125 --> 00:16:48,458
Just because I'm smiling
doesn't mean I'm happy.

252
00:16:49,666 --> 00:16:52,208
I might get beaten to death if I go home.

253
00:16:55,583 --> 00:16:57,125
I need to pack. I'm busy.

254
00:16:57,541 --> 00:16:58,625
Let's say goodbye here.

255
00:17:02,916 --> 00:17:06,041
And thank you. Truly.

256
00:17:08,958 --> 00:17:10,291
Are you sulking?

257
00:17:11,041 --> 00:17:12,041
Okay.

258
00:17:12,791 --> 00:17:14,416
Fine. Okay.

259
00:17:28,583 --> 00:17:30,875
When you said your mom hits you,

260
00:17:31,416 --> 00:17:33,750
I said I'm dealing
with a difficult mom too.

261
00:17:34,041 --> 00:17:35,291
Did you hate that so much?

262
00:17:35,666 --> 00:17:37,916
Just as you were born
without knowing your mom,

263
00:17:38,875 --> 00:17:41,625
I told you I was born that way too.
Did that upset you so much?

264
00:17:43,416 --> 00:17:44,916
That little brat.

265
00:17:45,541 --> 00:17:47,190
I should've killed her.

266
00:17:58,375 --> 00:17:59,836
Mom.

267
00:18:01,291 --> 00:18:02,583
Why are you here?

268
00:18:02,916 --> 00:18:04,208
Why are you looking for me?

269
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:05,958
I told you to do whatever you wanted.

270
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,930
- Mother, we can't do that.
- Why?

271
00:18:09,250 --> 00:18:11,291
Why do I suddenly matter to you?

272
00:18:11,916 --> 00:18:13,458
You all ignored me.

273
00:18:13,833 --> 00:18:16,291
We were wrong. We didn't think it through.

274
00:18:16,583 --> 00:18:19,250
If you need time, we'll wait.

275
00:18:19,583 --> 00:18:21,291
I won't do anything without you, Mother.

276
00:18:21,416 --> 00:18:22,457
Why the sudden change?

277
00:18:22,458 --> 00:18:24,125
I'm the one who wanted to rush things.

278
00:18:24,666 --> 00:18:25,708
Like I said,

279
00:18:25,833 --> 00:18:27,500
I'm tired of talking about marriage.

280
00:18:27,583 --> 00:18:29,458
I want to settle this and focus on work.

281
00:18:30,291 --> 00:18:31,666
Mom, don't you see how I feel?

282
00:18:31,708 --> 00:18:32,875
I do.

283
00:18:33,291 --> 00:18:35,708
Then get it settled and get back to work.

284
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,416
That's why I stepped aside.

285
00:18:37,458 --> 00:18:39,916
Mom! That's not what I mean!

286
00:18:48,041 --> 00:18:52,416
No family has ever accepted me
as their daughter.

287
00:18:53,166 --> 00:18:54,875
Don't start with that sad story.

288
00:18:55,250 --> 00:18:57,291
I want to be accepted
as a daughter-in-law.

289
00:18:58,041 --> 00:19:01,875
So take your time, Mother. I'll wait.

290
00:19:02,166 --> 00:19:04,375
Ji Hu said he'd wait with me too.

291
00:19:04,458 --> 00:19:06,166
So you're not changing your mind.

292
00:19:07,250 --> 00:19:12,458
So you want it all.
My son and my approval of you as his wife.

293
00:19:14,625 --> 00:19:16,500
I'd never wanted that before.

294
00:19:17,416 --> 00:19:21,208
To others, it might seem normal.
To me, it feels like asking too much.

295
00:19:21,291 --> 00:19:22,958
So I gave up before I even tried.

296
00:19:23,958 --> 00:19:25,125
But then,

297
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:29,500
outside Ji Hu's hospital room,
while he was fighting for his life,

298
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,250
I realized I wanted to try.

299
00:19:35,291 --> 00:19:38,333
Mother, please accept me.

300
00:19:39,333 --> 00:19:41,958
Please help me have a name of my own.

301
00:19:42,916 --> 00:19:44,125
I'll give it my all.

302
00:19:44,208 --> 00:19:45,958
I won't upset you.

303
00:19:46,916 --> 00:19:48,000
No.

304
00:19:48,375 --> 00:19:51,000
Why should I give you a name
even your own mom couldn't give you?

305
00:19:51,916 --> 00:19:54,708
You should never have been born.

306
00:19:56,791 --> 00:19:57,791
Stand up, please.

307
00:19:59,583 --> 00:20:03,125
- Mother.
- That's enough. You can both leave.

308
00:20:03,583 --> 00:20:05,291
I came here to let go.

309
00:20:06,416 --> 00:20:07,875
When I was raising my only son,

310
00:20:08,208 --> 00:20:10,958
I had expectations for his future wife.
I'm giving them all up.

311
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,125
Do whatever you two want.

312
00:20:12,291 --> 00:20:13,583
Don't come to me anymore.

313
00:20:14,583 --> 00:20:17,458
I'll take my time getting back.
Don't worry about me.

314
00:20:22,041 --> 00:20:23,333
Enough. Let's move forward.

315
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:24,708
Don't look back.

316
00:20:24,750 --> 00:20:25,916
Life lies ahead.

317
00:20:42,250 --> 00:20:43,583
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

318
00:20:43,625 --> 00:20:45,666
- This one, please.
- Of course. One moment.

319
00:20:52,750 --> 00:20:55,208
I'll pick these up.
You can help your customer.

320
00:20:55,375 --> 00:20:56,541
Who are you?

321
00:20:56,708 --> 00:20:58,250
Thanks, anyway.

322
00:21:09,625 --> 00:21:11,041
Sorry, who are you?

323
00:21:13,875 --> 00:21:15,207
Do you remember me?

324
00:21:15,208 --> 00:21:17,250
I'm Jung A, Ji Hu's friend.

325
00:21:17,416 --> 00:21:19,750
Ji Hu's mom gave us these shoes,

326
00:21:19,791 --> 00:21:23,375
but my mom wanted a different color,
so I came to exchange them.

327
00:21:24,583 --> 00:21:25,915
Is she out today?

328
00:21:25,916 --> 00:21:28,541
Yes, she had something to do at home.

329
00:21:30,666 --> 00:21:33,416
This is red ginseng.

330
00:21:33,875 --> 00:21:36,582
My mom said we couldn't accept
such a nice gift without giving back,

331
00:21:36,583 --> 00:21:38,000
so she sent this.

332
00:21:38,416 --> 00:21:40,375
- Thank her for me.
- I will.

333
00:21:41,791 --> 00:21:43,041
- Hello, Father.
- Hello.

334
00:21:43,083 --> 00:21:44,083
Dad.

335
00:21:44,416 --> 00:21:46,083
- Jung A.
- Hello.

336
00:21:46,666 --> 00:21:47,791
Welcome.

337
00:21:48,083 --> 00:21:49,625
Here you go. Take a look around.

338
00:21:49,666 --> 00:21:51,458
Mr. Im, I can help her.

339
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:53,625
I know these shoes really well.

340
00:21:53,791 --> 00:21:54,875
I'll let you talk.

341
00:21:57,916 --> 00:21:59,708
She's so quick-witted.

342
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:02,625
I saw Mom.

343
00:22:02,958 --> 00:22:04,416
She was at the vacation house.

344
00:22:04,833 --> 00:22:06,791
I figured she'd be there.

345
00:22:08,125 --> 00:22:10,500
- You've been through a lot.
- I'm fine.

346
00:22:11,708 --> 00:22:13,208
Do what you two planned.

347
00:22:13,291 --> 00:22:15,500
I'll convince your mom and bring her back.

348
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:18,625
- Dad.
- Go ahead.

349
00:22:19,541 --> 00:22:21,458
Waiting won't make any difference.

350
00:22:21,583 --> 00:22:22,791
Would that really be okay?

351
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:34,500
Seung Woo.

352
00:22:35,458 --> 00:22:36,458
You're asleep already?

353
00:22:37,750 --> 00:22:38,750
Are you sick?

354
00:23:03,416 --> 00:23:05,375
This guy, seriously...

355
00:23:14,916 --> 00:23:15,916
Yes, Mom.

356
00:23:17,458 --> 00:23:19,875
Seung Woo's home. He's asleep now.

357
00:23:20,416 --> 00:23:21,416
But, Mom,

358
00:23:22,583 --> 00:23:24,166
I think he really meant to go to London.

359
00:23:24,208 --> 00:23:25,583
- What?
- He's got a plane ticket.

360
00:23:26,083 --> 00:23:27,166
Unbelievable.

361
00:23:27,375 --> 00:23:30,125
He swore he didn't like her.
Why would he follow her there?

362
00:23:31,416 --> 00:23:34,291
Ji Ni really saved us.

363
00:23:34,333 --> 00:23:35,332
How did Ji Ni save us?

364
00:23:35,333 --> 00:23:38,954
Ji Ni said she wouldn't press charges
if Do Hee stopped seeing Seung Woo.

365
00:23:39,041 --> 00:23:41,583
She's saved us twice now.

366
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:43,500
Seung Hyun.

367
00:23:43,791 --> 00:23:47,166
You can't turn Ji Ni down.
Go with her to meet Ji Hu's family.

368
00:23:47,208 --> 00:23:48,916
I really don't want to.

369
00:23:49,250 --> 00:23:50,250
This time too...

370
00:23:50,875 --> 00:23:51,875
Anyway,

371
00:23:52,125 --> 00:23:53,958
I found out she was lying.

372
00:23:54,125 --> 00:23:55,250
Can you believe her nerve?

373
00:23:55,291 --> 00:23:57,750
Am I just there for show?

374
00:23:58,041 --> 00:23:59,333
You always tell me to just sit there.

375
00:23:59,375 --> 00:24:01,583
What did she lie about?

376
00:24:02,250 --> 00:24:04,916
Seung Hyun, forget about Se Ri.

377
00:24:05,083 --> 00:24:06,500
Do it for Ji Ni.

378
00:24:07,833 --> 00:24:08,958
Okay.

379
00:24:25,791 --> 00:24:28,333
I never thought I'd see this day.

380
00:24:30,250 --> 00:24:33,791
Honey, I wish you were here.

381
00:24:51,833 --> 00:24:54,250
Thanks. I know I can count on you.

382
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:58,375
I'll do my best.

383
00:24:58,541 --> 00:25:01,416
I really thought I was doing
what was best for you.

384
00:25:02,041 --> 00:25:03,041
Forget it.

385
00:25:07,333 --> 00:25:08,666
Thank you.

386
00:25:15,125 --> 00:25:19,083
You even have to thank your own brother
for coming to meet the in-laws.

387
00:25:19,416 --> 00:25:20,541
Poor thing.

388
00:25:22,166 --> 00:25:23,458
I'm sorry, Ji Ni.

389
00:25:24,041 --> 00:25:26,875
When you have your own papers,
you can live with your head held high.

390
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:45,791
You're wearing that? It's not a funeral.

391
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:47,500
I'm as good as dead today.

392
00:25:48,208 --> 00:25:50,625
Well, at least you're going.

393
00:25:51,375 --> 00:25:53,583
You'll wear comfortable shoes, right?

394
00:26:04,666 --> 00:26:06,958
Seriously?

395
00:26:58,958 --> 00:27:01,666
Ji Ni, I'm nervous.

396
00:27:03,166 --> 00:27:04,875
What are you nervous about?

397
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:55,000
Did you just come from a funeral?

398
00:27:55,500 --> 00:27:57,104
Did you just come from a festival?

399
00:28:34,291 --> 00:28:37,333
(Family Register)

400
00:28:37,541 --> 00:28:38,875
I want to move in with you.

401
00:28:38,916 --> 00:28:40,749
No. Who said you could move in?

402
00:28:40,750 --> 00:28:42,541
The statute of limitations has expired.

403
00:28:42,583 --> 00:28:43,999
Lies have no statute of limitations.

404
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:45,040
Don't get involved.

405
00:28:45,041 --> 00:28:48,665
Build a real family of your own. Be happy.

406
00:28:48,666 --> 00:28:49,790
How did you find out?

407
00:28:49,791 --> 00:28:51,374
First, let's find out where they live now.

408
00:28:51,375 --> 00:28:52,874
Don't you remember me? Pumseongak.

409
00:28:52,875 --> 00:28:54,624
Pay me, or I'll turn myself in right now.

410
00:28:54,625 --> 00:28:56,500
And I'll drag you into it too.

411
00:28:57,799 --> 00:28:59,799
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
